>> title: Almond Biscotti
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: almond, italian, twice baked, coffee, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: biscotti, cantucci, cantuccini, biscotti di Prato
>> servings: 24
>> time: 1 hour 30 min
>> step.6: shape into two logs, bake 350°F (175°C) 25 min
>> step.7: slice 3/4 in thick, bake 325°F (165°C) 20 min

Heat the #oven{} to 350°F (175°C) and line a #baking sheet{} with parchment.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{2%cup}(250 g), @granulated sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g), @baking powder{1 1/2%tsp}(7 g), and @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g).

Beat @eggs{2%large}(100 g) with @melted butter{6%Tbs}(85 g), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL), and @almond extract{1/2%tsp}(2.5 mL).

Stir @&(~1)egg mixture{} into @&(~2)dry ingredients{}.

Fold @whole almonds{1%cup}(140 g; toasted) into @&(~1)dough{}.

Shape @&(~1)dough{} into two logs and bake at 350°F for ~{25%min}.

Slice @&(~1)logs{} 3/4 in thick and bake at 325°F for ~{20%min}.
